{"id":"14D","title":"Forbidden Foods and Practices","part":{"n":14,"title":"Food and health laws"},"url":"/law/14-food-and-health-laws/14d","entries":[{"id":"14D.1","text":"You shall not eat anything which dies of itself.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":14,"verses":"21"}],"citation":"Deut. 14:21."},{"id":"14D.2","text":"That which dies of itself may be given or sold to foreigners.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":14,"verses":"21"}],"citation":"Deut. 14:21."},{"id":"14D.3","text":"One who eats any animal that died of itself shall wash his clothes and bathe, and will be unclean until evening; otherwise he will bear his iniquity.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":17,"verses":"15-16"}],"citation":"Lev. 17:15-16."},{"id":"14D.4","text":"You shall eat no manner of fat from any animal.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":3,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":7,"verses":"23-25"}],"citation":"Lev. 3:17; Lev. 7:23-25."},{"id":"14D.5","text":"You shall not eat any abominable thing.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":14,"verses":"3"}],"citation":"Deut. 14:3."},{"id":"14D.6","text":"You shall not eat any manner of blood from fowl or beast either by itself or with its flesh.","refs":[{"book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":3,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":7,"verses":"26-27"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":17,"verses":"10-14"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"26"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":12,"verses":"16,23-25"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":15,"verses":"23"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":15,"verses":"20,29"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":21,"verses":"25"}],"citation":"Gen. 9:4; Lev. 3:17; Lev. 7:26-27; Lev. 17:10-14; Lev. 19:26; Deut 12:16, 23-25; Deut 15:23; Acts 15:20, 29; Acts 21:25."},{"id":"14D.7","text":"You are not to boil a kid in the milk of its mother.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"26"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":14,"verses":"21"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:19; Exod. 34:26; Deut. 14:21."},{"id":"14D.8","text":"Abstain from animals that were strangled.","refs":[{"book":"Acts","chapter":15,"verses":"20-9"}],"citation":"Acts 15:20-9; 21:25."},{"id":"14D.9","text":"Admonished not to drink strong drink and become drunk.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":10,"verses":"9"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":13,"verses":"13"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":6,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Lev. 10:9; Rom. 13:13; 1 Cor. 6:10."},{"id":"14D.10","text":"You shall not eat any flesh that is torn of beasts in the field, you shall cast it to the dogs.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":22,"verses":"31"}],"citation":"Exod. 22:31."},{"id":"14D.11","text":"Admonishment against gluttony and overeating.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":23,"verses":"1-3,20-21"},{"book":"Philippians","chapter":3,"verses":"18,19"}],"citation":"Prov. 23:1-3, 20-21; Phil. 3:18, 19."}]}